Package: corrplotng
Title: Next Generation Correlation Plots
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("corrplot-ng contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "maintainers@example.invalid")
Description: An R adapter for corrplot-ng. It retains a legacy-compatible
    plotting path through the upstream corrplot package and provides an
    experimental scene-v1 preparation path, a Rust-backed SVG renderer,
    normalized matrix and file input adapters, pairwise correlation testing,
    and palette/color-legend helpers. The scene path prepares renderer-neutral
    data; the Rust renderer supports a documented subset of scene-v1 output.
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    corrplot (>= 0.95),
    utils
Suggests:
    jsonlite,
    png,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager) (>= 1.78.0), rustc (>= 1.78.0), xz
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
Config/testthat/edition: 3
